# Copy to .env on the box. Every key the code reads is listed; unset means the default.
#
# THE MONEY SWITCHES AND THE BOOK SWITCHES APPLY WITHOUT A RESTART. Edit this file and the
# running bot picks the change up within a second: it logs what moved, records the seam, and
# republishes the strategy the monitors read. A position already open keeps the rules it
# opened under; the new values apply to the next entry. Anything invalid is REFUSED whole,
# with the previous values left running, so a typo cannot resize a trade.
#
# The rest of the keys are captured when the process starts and a change to one is reported
# but NOT applied, because the object built from it already exists (a client, the signer, an
# open database, a bound port). src/config/schema.ts is the list, and it is the only list.
#
# For a hot key this FILE beats the environment, on purpose: pm2 replays its own saved copy
# of the environment on every `pm2 restart --update-env`, and on 2026-09-06 a stale
# TRADE_SIZE_ETH from pm2 silently beat an edit made here. For a restart key the environment
# still wins, so `MODE=observe DB_FILE=... pm2 start` keeps working.

# burner EOA private key (0x-prefixed). NEVER commit the real one.
PRIVATE_KEY=0x

# ---- money switches ----
# broadcast gate. MODE=live AND LIVE=1 is real money; anything else signs without sending.
MODE=shadow
LIVE=0
# stop entering, keep exiting. HALT=0 is a money decision, asked for on its own.
HALT=0
TRADE_SIZE_ETH=0.005
BANKROLL_ETH=0.020
# The creator-tax band the book buys, bps, both ends inclusive. Hot: edit and save, no
# restart. 50/10000 is the band the bot ran from 2026-08-28. 0/0 buys untaxed launches and
# nothing else, which is a different policy, not a looser version of the same one. Neither
# bound touches the book screen (STRATEGY.maxCreatorTaxBps, 200bps), so every launch stays
# observed and the daily edge check keeps its control group either way.
ENTRY_MIN_TAX_BPS=50
ENTRY_MAX_TAX_BPS=10000
# THE BOOKS. Blank means one book from the two keys above, which is exactly the behaviour
# that shipped before this key existed. Set it to run more than one band side by side:
#
#   BOOKS=untaxed:0-0,taxed:50-10000
#
# name:minBps-maxBps, comma separated, up to 4, names alphanumeric. The bands must NOT
# overlap: a launch has one creator tax, so a disjoint set means it routes to exactly one
# book and can never be bought twice. Overlapping bands are refused at load, not merged.
# Setting this together with ENTRY_MIN_TAX_BPS or ENTRY_MAX_TAX_BPS is also refused, because
# the band would then be declared in two places and the published one could differ from the
# traded one. Each book carries its own MAX_DRAWDOWN_ETH, so see MAX_WALLET_DRAWDOWN_ETH.
BOOKS=
# The kill switch, in ETH from the peak. Same unit as TRADE_SIZE_ETH on purpose: divided by
# the trade size this IS the stake multiple, and the stake multiple is what the replays fit
# (3 stakes = 0.06 ETH at a 0.02 size, which is what the box runs). It was MAX_DRAWDOWN_USD
# until 2026-09-07, which coupled the stop to ETHUSD: a configured 2145 against a real 2515
# made a "$240" limit really $282. It fires from the peak, then lifts ITSELF once the venue
# has paid again over DD_RESUME_WINDOW launches scored since it fired, at most twice a UTC
# day; resetting the accounting is part of the lift. `npm run newepoch -- "why"` moves it
# by hand.
#
# Retained after the current-size audit. The previous mixed-size optimization
# claims were not independently validated. This limit can be exceeded across resets.
MAX_DRAWDOWN_ETH=0.06

# THE WALLET-WIDE STOP, the OTHER drawdown. MAX_DRAWDOWN_ETH above is an accounting figure
# over closed positions and splits per book; this one is compared against the real wallet
# balance and cannot be attributed to a book at all. Blank or 0 derives it as
# books x MAX_DRAWDOWN_ETH, which with one book is MAX_DRAWDOWN_ETH, i.e. unchanged. It is
# refused below MAX_DRAWDOWN_ETH: if the wallet stop fired first, no book could ever reach
# its own limit and per-book drawdown would look like it worked while doing nothing.
MAX_WALLET_DRAWDOWN_ETH=
# The resumable daily cap was DELETED on 2026-09-07. It could not lift before 00:00 UTC,
# and on 2026-09-05 it would have tripped at 06:35 and sat out $731 of that day's replay.
# The drawdown stop above, which lifts itself on the venue's own scores, is what binds.
# Finalized 2026-09-07 from the current-size guard audit. This is an operating
# choice with limited prospective evidence, not a proven optimum.
# Pause below -1 simulated stake over 20 scored book launches; reopen above +1.
# The whole window must fit inside three hours. Stale evidence can release a pause.
VENUE_PAUSE_WINDOW=20
VENUE_PAUSE_OFF=-1
VENUE_PAUSE_ON=1
VENUE_FRESH_H=3
# Enabled only by the verified release cutover. It never falls back to a fixed-bar sensor.
VENUE_EXECUTION_SCENARIOS=0
# What the drawdown stop needs before it lifts itself: this many launches scored SINCE it
# fired, summing above DD_RESUME_ON stakes. At 13.1 buyable launches an hour, 20 is about
# 90 minutes.
#
# Recovery requires strictly above +1 stake, matching market-pause recovery.
# The twice-per-day budget survives process restarts.
DD_RESUME_WINDOW=20
DD_RESUME_ON=1
# Halt when our own returns come in this many points per trade below what the same coins
# replayed at, over the last 20 trades. That is a bug in us, not a market, so it never
# lifts itself: a restart is the lift.
BROKEN_GAP_PP=15
# The entry clock (ENTRY_UTC_HOURS, 12-24 UTC) was DELETED on 2026-09-07. It was measured
# and real -- 00-12 UTC was 10 of 18 day-blocks negative while 12-24 was +0.20 with 0 of 13
# negative -- but by 09-06 it kept only 73% of September's profit with six of seven nights
# positive, and the venue pause plus the self-lifting drawdown stop replaced it. What
# survives is WS_HOURS below, which is the same predicate doing the OTHER job it had.
# The untaxed probe book was DELETED on 2026-09-07. It traded candidate filters at a tenth
# the size under its own cap so replay results got calibrated by real fills; its last
# standing verdict was "not paying" (55 real trades, -$6.81) and it had been off since
# 09-06. positions.cohort survives it, because history has probe rows at a tenth the size
# that must keep being excluded from the real-vs-replay comparison.

# ---- chain access ----
# Alchemy key as a websocket url. Launch subscription inside the entry window, and the
# https form is derived from it for the two per-launch reads (RPC_KEY_URL overrides).
# Leave EMPTY rather than half-filled; a placeholder just 401s in a loop. To park the
# socket, rename the key to LOGS_WS_URL_PARKED and restart.
LOGS_WS_URL=
# Leave unset on the free tier: eth_getLogs is capped at 10 blocks there and billed per
# byte, so the poller stays on the public rpc.
# RPC_URL=
# RPC_KEY_URL=

# Disabled by default. While STOP ALL is set and the wallet is fully quiet, poll logs on the
# public RPC first. START restores paid polling and completes a keyed catch-up before resuming.
RPC_STOPPED_ECONOMY=0
RPC_HALTED_ECONOMY=0 # Public polling when every book is halted and the wallet is flat. Overrides RPC_STOPPED_ECONOMY.

# which file the bot reads this config from. A second instance that needs its own money
# switches points this at its own file; unset means .env beside the process.
# ENV_FILE=.env

# ---- the event tape ----
# Where the append-only event tape is recorded. THE PATH IS THE SWITCH: unset means no
# recorder at all, so there is no second boolean that can disagree with it.
#
# RECORDING ONLY. It observes and never decides. Nothing in a trading path reads it, no
# trading code awaits it, and a recording failure never halts trading: losing an event
# costs reproducibility, not correctness. Retention is 14 days OR 1 GB, whichever bites
# first, and beneath both a 2 GB free-disk floor stops recording rather than filling the
# box. The SQLite work happens in a forked writer that is started with no key.
#
# It exists so the rewrite can prove itself: the unconfirmed sequencer-feed overlay that
# every entry price and every exit mark is computed from is recorded nowhere else, so
# without this no replay can reproduce a live decision.
# TAPE_DB=data/tape.db

# ---- gate and data ----
# 1: the in-process cohort ring decides the regime halt (verdict ~47s after the launch);
# 0/unset: gatewatch.py's five-minute file decides. gatewatch keeps writing either way.
# Hours the Alchemy socket and the provider key are used (from-to UTC, wrap allowed).
# Blank = always, which is the live setting. A QUOTA lever, not a trading rule: a launch
# outside these hours is entered exactly the same way, just discovered by the poller and
# read through the public rpc. The key is 30M compute units a month and the bot was on
# pace for 36M on 2026-09-07, so this is the switch to reach for.
# WS_HOURS=
GATE_LIVE=1
# GATE_DB=data/gate.db
# DB_FILE=data/bot.db          # a second instance needs its own file
# DASH=1  DASH_PORT=8787
# REBASELINE=1                 # one boot only, after a top-up or withdrawal
# ETHUSD=2515                  # boot seed and offline fallback for the ETH price. DISPLAY
#                               # ONLY since 2026-09-07: no stop reads it, which is what
#                               # makes it safe for the bot to refresh it hourly and
#                               # publish it to chain_truth.eth_usd for every script.
# REQUIRE_DEV_BUY=1            # reject launches whose creator buy cannot be read
# PONS_TERMINAL_URL=           # the venue's UI, linked from the dashboard's exit rows
# Adaptive matched shadow indicator and fresh recovery. Requires prospective verification.
VENUE_FRESH_RECOVERY=0
